      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-07T11:27:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The permission check is in `debug_access_allowed`, which current only allows calls from UIDs 0 or 2000 (the shell user). If there\u0027s a better way to do it I\u0027m happy to change that, but there didn\u0027t seem to be any obvious documentation.\n\nIt\u0027s used for the `list` command of the `vm` tool, for debugging.\n\nI\u0027m not familiar with DUMP_TRANSACTION. Where can I read more about it and the standard permission check you mention?\n\nThere were added in https://r.android.com/1660251 on David\u0027s request, so it might be better to discuss there.",
      "parentUuid": "d35eb020_283651d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "b8f1e9608fa330e3f466ef0d6459d03b6d4de676",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
